    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7-a1">

                <pb facs="0053" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg11"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 20,1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, her Britannic Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign
                    affairs, has the honor to acquaint Mr. Adams, envoy extraordinary and minister
                    plenipotentiary of the United States at this court, that her Majesty’s <pb
                        facs="0054" n="12" xml:id="pg12"/> government are informed by persons, to
                    whom they are disposed to give credit, that recruits are being raised in this
                    country for service in the army of the United States, and that bounty money of a
                    considerable amount is offered by agents of the United States to encourage
                    British subjects to enlist.</p>
                <p>Mr. Adams must be well aware that any of her Majesty’s subjects enlisting in the
                    military service of either of the belligerent parties in America, or any persons
                    procuring any of her Majesty’s subjects to enlist in that service, are guilty of
                    a misdemeanor according to British law; and Mr. Adams will readily see that such
                    a practice as that to which the undersigned now calls his attention is
                    calculated seriously to increase the difficulties already incident to the
                    observance of neutrality by her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>The undersigned requests Mr. Adams to receive the assurance of his highest
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
